From: Jarvis <jarvis@khaan.si>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: declare airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available before first use

9999-15 calls airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available() in
airoha_ppe_debugfs_foe_show() but defines it as static further down
the same file. Since Linux 6.8 the kernel build treats an implicit
function declaration as a hard error
(-Werror=implicit-function-declaration), so any build with
CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y fails here:

  drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c:172: implicit
  declaration of function 'airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available'
  drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c:234: conflicting
  types for 'airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available'

Add a forward declaration before the first use; the definition is
left untouched. Drop this patch if upstream fixes 9999-15 itself.

Signed-off-by: Jarvis <jarvis@khaan.si>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
@@ -37,6 +37,13 @@
 		seq_printf(m, ":%d", *dest_port);
 }
 
+/* airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available() is defined below
+ * airoha_ppe_debugfs_foe_show(); declare it here so the first use does
+ * not trigger an implicit-function-declaration error, which has been a
+ * hard error since Linux 6.8 (-Werror=implicit-function-declaration).
+ */
+static bool airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available(struct airoha_ppe *ppe);
+
 static int airoha_ppe_debugfs_foe_show(struct seq_file *m, void *private,
 				       bool bind)
 {
